g $i^{-1}=-i$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9008a7d73dd9633157e3d11c"},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-reciprocal-html-q14","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which equation verifies that $w$ is the reciprocal of $z$?","options":["$z+w=0$","$zw=1$","$w=\\overline z$","$|w|=|z|$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"61e564ae1e2f18ab2a613118"},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-reciprocal-html-q15","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"When is $z^{-1}=\\overline z$?","options":["When $z=0$","When $z$ is real and nonzero only","For every complex number","When $|z|=1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"57773e383b17cee74fa773aa"},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-reciprocal-html-q16","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $z=3+4\\mathrm i$, what is $z^{-1}$?","options":["$\\frac3{25}+\\frac4{25}\\mathrm i$","$\\frac3{25}-\\frac4{25}\\mathrm i$","$3-4\\mathrm i$","$\\frac14-\\frac13\\mathrm i$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1a86ce89dedd84ef0beed12e"},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-reciprocal-html-q17","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is the condition $z\\ne0$ essential in $z^{-1}=\\overline z/|z|^2$?","options":["Because $\\overline0$ is undefined.","Because $0$ has two different reciprocals.","Because $0^{-1}=0$ only in the complex plane.","Because $|0|^2=0$, so the formula would divide by zero."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e3aeecc562234ee7f58b3f7b"},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-reciprocal-html-q18","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $z=2e^{i\\pi/3}$, which polar form represents $z^{-1}$?","options":["$2e^{-i\\pi/3}$","$\\frac12e^{i\\pi/3}$","$4e^{i\\pi/3}$","$\\frac12e^{-i\\pi/3}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"395385d05bc61f04e8ee7b20"},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-compl